{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rubellite-condensed-bettong","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Three follow-ups on the unit-tier subprocess-isolation guard, all raised as non-blocking advisories\nby the LLM code review on Gerrit 2506 and deferred there.\n\n1. _check_home_escape may OVER-FLAG. It treats any argv element referencing a name or attribute in\n   _HOME_ESCAPE_NAMES (home, mkdtemp, TemporaryDirectory) as a hazard. An unrelated local named\n   `home`, or a tmp_path-rooted mkdtemp that is perfectly harnessed, would be reported. Zero live\n   sites hit it today, so it is latent rather than active — but the guard s whole design premise is\n   that a false positive is as costly as a false negative, because reddening innocent files is how a\n   guard gets reverted. Narrow it to the attribute forms that actually escape (Path.home(),\n   os.environ[\"HOME\"]) and add both a positive and a negative case.\n2. The UsageError contract is verified only by GREPPING conftest.py text for the string within a\n   window. That asserts the source, not the behaviour: it would pass if the arm raised something\n   else while the word appeared nearby. The contract matters (from the xdist controller a\n   pytest.fail escapes as a 20-line INTERNALERROR), so it deserves a real assertion on the raised\n   type.\n3. The file-level opt-out fallback for hazards found in MODULE-LEVEL HELPERS is untested. That path\n   exists so a marked test s shared helper is covered when the finding carries no test name of its\n   own; five live sites rely on it via a module pytestmark. It was verified once by hand during\n   implementation and never pinned.\n\nSee tests/_subprocess_isolation.py and tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py.","id":"c678-e73c-b48a-4bbe","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Narrow the isolation guard's home-escape rule and pin two untested contracts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788330600560697001,"uuid":"366f4732-6859-4031-9686-b0fe5d20df25"}